  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RS! Global Linking &amp; Learning REC LATAM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The core underlying principle of the learning agenda is to identify solutions that can bring about systemic change across the supply chains where we work, looking at the roles that the private sector, the public sector and civic society need to play to generate impact on core strategic areas of Decent Work, Climate &amp; Natural Resource Management, Fair Value Distribution and Sustainable Consumption.  

Five thematic learning teams, each with a thematic learning and innovation plan, agenda, and sufficient resources conduct research, gather evidence from the field, engage with experts from several local members of the RSC and partners, and learn together around the core issues in relation to the above themes in the value chain.</narrative>
  </description>
